      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The amendment says a failed plain INSERT makes `last_insert_rowid()` known, but `insertCounts` and `Counters.apply` preserve its previous value, possibly unknown, when the first row fails or the table is `WITHOUT ROWID`. Fix: state that the counter becomes known only when a row was inserted into a rowid table before the failure; otherwise it retains its previous value."
